<title>USA: Fed refrains from open market operations.</title>
<headline>Fed refrains from open market operations.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve refrained from open market operations on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Fed's absence from the market was in line with most Wall Street analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>At 1130 EDT/1530 GMT, the time the Fed usually intervenes in the market, the federal funds rate stood at 5-1/8 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
